abstract:
We study the existence problem for positive solutions $u \in L^{r}(\mathbb{R}^{n})$, $0<r<\infty$, to the quasilinear elliptic equation \[ -Δ_{p} u = σu^{q} \quad 	ext{in} \;\; \mathbb{R}^n \] in the sub-natural growth case $0<q< p-1$, where $Δ_{p}u = 	ext{div}( |
abla u|^{p-2} 
abla u )$ is the $p$-Laplacian with $1<p<\infty$, and $σ$ is a nonnegative measurable function (or measure) on $\mathbb{R}^n$. Our techniques rely on a study of general integral equations involving nonlinear potentials and related weighted norm inequalities. They are applicable to more general quasilinear elliptic operators such as the $\mathcal{A}$-Laplacian $	ext{div} \mathcal{A}(x,
abla u)$, and the fractional Laplacian $(-Δ)^α$ on $\mathbb{R}^n$, as well as linear uniformly elliptic operators with bounded measurable coefficients $	ext{div}(\mathcal{A} 
abla u)$ on an arbitrary domain $Ω\subseteq \mathbb{R}^n$ with a positive Green function.

In this article, the authors consider the Schrödinger type operator $L:=-{m div}(A
abla)+V$ on $\mathbb{R}^n$ with $n\geq 3$, where the matrix $A$ satisfies uniformly elliptic condition and the nonnegative potential $V$ belongs to the reverse Hölder class $RH_q(\mathbb{R}^n)$ with $q\in(n/2,\,\infty)$. Let $p(\cdot):\ \mathbb{R}^n	o(0,\,\infty)$ be a variable exponent function satisfying the globally $\log$-Hölder continuous condition. When $p(\cdot):\ \mathbb{R}^n	o(1,\,\infty)$, the authors prove that the operators $VL^{-1}$, $V^{1/2}
abla L^{-1}$ and $
abla^2L^{-1}$ are bounded on variable Lebesgue space $L^{p(\cdot)}(\mathbb{R}^n)$. When $p(\cdot):\ \mathbb{R}^n	o(0,\,1]$, the authors introduce the variable Hardy space $H_L^{p(\cdot)}(\mathbb{R}^n)$, associated to $L$, and show that $VL^{-1}$, $V^{1/2}
abla L^{-1}$ and $
abla^2L^{-1}$ are bounded from $H_L^{p(\cdot)}(\mathbb{R}^n)$ to $L^{p(\cdot)}(\mathbb{R}^n)$.
